On Thursday, February 21, 2013 11:16:33 AM UTC-5, Bob Carpenter wrote:<blockquote class="gmail_quote" style="margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex">On 2/21/13 2:52 AM, Ben Goodrich wrote:
<br>&gt; On Monday, February 18, 2013 2:28:28 AM UTC-5, Ben Goodrich wrote:
<br>&gt;
<br>&gt;     -- There are more (relevant) coefficient-wise operations defined for Eigen objects than for std::vectors. This link
<br>&gt;     has many of them
<br>&gt;
<br>&gt;     <a href="http://eigen.tuxfamily.org/dox/AsciiQuickReference.txt" target="_blank" rel="nofollow" data-saferedirecturl="https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://eigen.tuxfamily.org/dox/AsciiQuickReference.txt&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792477229893000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3IViPjaRuKgI2rgY33ssJv">http://eigen.tuxfamily.org/dox/AsciiQuickReference.txt</a> &lt;<a href="http://eigen.tuxfamily.org/dox/AsciiQuickReference.txt" target="_blank" rel="nofollow" data-saferedirecturl="https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://eigen.tuxfamily.org/dox/AsciiQuickReference.txt&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792477229893000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3IViPjaRuKgI2rgY33ssJv">http://eigen.tuxfamily.org/dox/AsciiQuickReference.txt</a>&gt;
<br>&gt;
<br>&gt;     Most of the STL operations (sorting, etc.) are not that common in statistical applications.
<br>&gt;
<br>&gt;
<br>&gt; Another thing that is possible but not urgent is that if more things in Stan were based on Eigen, then maybe stanc could
<br>&gt; parse the method operator literally, so that
<br>&gt;
<br>&gt; |
<br>&gt; X.foo().bar();
<br>&gt; |
<br>&gt;
<br>&gt; would work if foo and bar were methods defined in Eigen. Even better would be for the .cpp file that stanc generates to
<br>&gt; #include EIGEN_MATRIXBASE_PLUGIN so that users could define foo and bar.
<br>
<br>That was a bit abstract for me.  Do you mean that &quot;X.foo().bar()&quot; would be
<br>valid Stan syntax and we&#39;d just translate it to C++ directly?
<br></blockquote>
